# J.A.R.V.I.S. — MARK LV

JARVIS is a Windows desktop voice assistant powered by Google's Gemini Live API.
It can listen and respond in real time, use voice-controlled tools, and provide
a graphical assistant interface. An internet connection and a Gemini API key
are required for AI conversations; JARVIS is not an offline language model.

## What JARVIS can do

- Have live voice conversations, with microphone and speaker selection, mute,
  push-to-talk, and optional wake-word mode.
- Use tools for web search, browser control, app and system actions, reminders,
  file and document tasks, and media playback.
- Use built-in actions and optional plugins that can be enabled in the app.
- Keep personal long-term memory locally on the PC.
- Offer an optional phone-friendly dashboard on the local network.
- Open the local Content Studio page in your browser. Its Video Editor tile
  links to the online editor at 123apps.

Some tools need compatible hardware or software. Browser control typically
needs Chrome or Edge installed on the PC. Camera features need a camera.

## Requirements

- Windows 10 or 11, 64-bit.
- Internet access and a Gemini API key.
- A microphone and speakers/headphones for voice conversations.
- No separate Python installation or dedicated GPU is required.

## Install on Windows

1. Download [JARVIS-Setup-x64.exe](./Mark-LV-main/dist/JARVIS-Setup-x64.exe).
2. Run the installer and follow its prompts. It installs for the current
   Windows user under Local AppData, so administrator access and a separate
   Python installation are not required.
3. Use the Start menu shortcut to launch JARVIS. You can also choose the
   optional desktop shortcut during installation.
4. On first launch, enter your Gemini API key. You can create one in
   [Google AI Studio](https://aistudio.google.com/apikey).
5. Select the microphone and speakers you want JARVIS to use, then check that
   Windows allows microphone access for desktop apps.

Keep your API key private. It is stored locally with the app's configuration.
Conversation content is sent to Google's Gemini service when you use AI
features. Long-term memory is stored locally on the PC. By default, the
configuration is under `%LOCALAPPDATA%\Programs\JARVIS\config\` and memory is
under `%LOCALAPPDATA%\Programs\JARVIS\memory\`.

The installer is currently unsigned, so Windows may display a SmartScreen
warning. Only run it if you trust where you downloaded it from.

## First-use notes

- Keep an internet connection available for Gemini and web-based tools.
- Install Chrome or Edge if you want to use browser-control tools. Playwright
  browser binaries are not included in the installer.
- The phone dashboard is optional and is intended for use on the same local
  network as the PC. Windows Firewall may ask you to allow network access.
- Wake-word mode is optional and may need to download its model when enabled.

## Uninstall

Uninstall **JARVIS - MARK LV** from **Settings > Apps > Installed apps**.
Back up anything important in the app's configuration or memory folders before
uninstalling or moving to another PC.

## Build the installer (developers)

From the project directory, install the runtime dependencies and run the
PowerShell build script:

```powershell
python -m pip install -r requirements.txt
.\build.ps1
```

The build PC needs Python and Inno Setup 6. The finished installer is written
to `dist\JARVIS-Setup-x64.exe`. People installing the finished setup do not
need Python or Inno Setup.